# ALLOWLIST — ignore everything, then re-include only what the image needs.
#
# A denylist ("exclude .env") only protects against secrets someone thought of in
# advance. With an allowlist, any new file — .env.prod, a *.pem key, a token dump,
# a backup — is kept out of the build context by default and can never reach an
# image layer. If you add a runtime file, add a matching "!" line below.
*
!*.py
!requirements.txt

# Belt and braces: nothing above re-includes these, but keep them denied explicitly
# in case the allowlist is ever loosened.
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*token*.json
secrets/
.git
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
